  "source": {
    "title": "T7000 Thermostat Modbus Data Table",
    "doc_number": "Revision 2.4",
    "revision_date": "2019-12-23",
    "url": "https://docs.johnsoncontrols.com/bas/api/khub/documents/hw6JWFAKzTKFpujvU7eW7g/content",
    "pages": "p. 2 (interface, coils), pp. 3-7 (input and holding registers, notes and demo frames), pp. 8-9 (model and output mapping)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Supported functions 01, 03, 04, 06 and 16. Holding registers 1-4 repeat input registers 1-4.",
    "All temperatures are x10 (26.5 °C is stored as 265).",
    "Left out: sample time, P and I (registers 34-36) and AO2/AI (45), whose footnote says they are x10 values while their printed ranges read like plain integers; the sensor offset (22), because its -5 to 5 °C range needs a signed encoding the table never states; register 27 was deleted in revision 2.2.",
    "Many registers apply only to some models (marked in descriptions). Relay roles per model/application are in the output mapping table of the source.",
    "Address range 1-64; baud 9600 or 4800 (the table does not say which is the default); 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit."
  ],
